    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All green. Build succeeds and both the targeted household test and the full suite pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `householdId` is now a deterministic function of `(normalizedLastName, postcode)`, and the household-keyed behaviours all follow from it. Changes, kept as small cohesive edits so structural impact stays low:\n\n- **`IdentityKey.java`** \u2014 made `household(lastName, postcode)` the single public source of truth: first 12 hex chars of `SHA-256(normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode)`, null when there's no postcode. `forRequest` now computes it unconditionally (no longer gated on `sharesHousehold`). All other consumers delegate here, so the derivation lives in one place.\n- **`AssignHousehold.java`** \u2014 collapsed to always set the computed id from the owner's own last name + postcode. No more `sharesHousehold` gate and no per-owner linking loop (deterministic ids mean same-household owners converge automatically).\n- **`RejectDuplicateHousehold.java`** \u2014 now rejects (409) when the request's computed `householdId` already exists on another owner; `sharesHousehold=true` bypasses it (declared member), and no postcode means no household so it's skipped. **Wired into `owners.POST.yml`** between the identity check and the capacity check.\n- **`FlagPossibleDuplicate.java`** \u2014 keys off the computed `householdId` (equality) instead of re-deriving lastName+postcode, and skips declared members (`sharesHousehold=true`), since a declared member is not a suspected duplicate.\n\n`HouseholdTier` (the membership-level GOLD upgrade) already read `owner.getHouseholdId()`, so it now correctly sizes households off the computed id with no edit needed. The `sharesHousehold` flag now only bypasses the duplicate block rather than creating the link, exactly as specified.\n\nNet: 4 Java files + 1 YAML touched, each changed function small and low-complexity.",
